 'Vigilance\\nCycling {1} ({1}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Vigilance\\nWhen Farfinder enters the battlefield, you may search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'When Bastion of Remembrance enters the battlefield, create a 1/1 white Human Soldier creature token.\\nWhenever a creature you control dies, each opponent loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.', 'When Daysquad Marshal enters the battlefield, create a 1/1 white Human Soldier creature token.', 'When Duskfang Mentor enters the battlefield, put a lifelink counter on target non-Human creature you control.\\n{1}{B}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control with lifelink.', "When Frillscare Mentor enters the battlefield, put a menace counter on target non-Human creature you control. (It can't be blocked except by two or more creatures.)\\n{2}{R}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control with menace.", "When Frost Lynx enters the battlefield, tap target creature an opponent controls. That creature doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", 'When Garrison Cat dies, create a 1/1 white Human Soldier creature token.', 'When Honey Mammoth enters the battlefield, you gain 4 life.', 'When Hornbash Mentor enters the battlefield, put a trample counter on target non-Human creature you control.\\n{2}{G}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control with trample.', 'When Keensight Mentor enters the battlefield, put a vigilance counter on target non-Human creature you control.\\n{1}{W}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control with vigilance.', "When Kogla, the Titan Ape enters the battlefield, it fights up to one target creature you don't control.\\nWhenever Kogla attacks, destroy target artifact or enchantment defending player controls.\\n{1}{G}: Return target Human you control to its owner's hand. Kogla gains indestructible until end of turn.", 'When Nightsquad Commando enters the battlefield, if you attacked this turn, create a 1/1 white Human Soldier creature token.', 'When Rooting Moloch enters the battlefield, exile target card with a cycling ability from your graveyard. Until the end of your next turn, you may play that card.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'When Serrated Scorpion dies, it deals 2 damage to each opponent and you gain 2 life.', "When Sleeper Dart enters the battlefield, draw a card.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Sleeper Dart: Target creature doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", 'When Wingspan Mentor enters the battlefield, put a flying counter on target non-Human creature you control.\\n{2}{U}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control with flying.', "Whenever Exuberant Wolfbear attacks, you may change the base power and toughness of target Human you control to Exuberant Wolfbear's power and toughness until end of turn.", "Whenever Momentum Rumbler attacks, if it doesn't have first strike, put a first strike counter on it.\\nWhenever Momentum Rumbler attacks, if it has first strike, it gains double strike until end of turn.", 'Whenever Perimeter Sergeant attacks, other Humans you control get +1/+0 until end of turn.', "Whenever Phase Dolphin attacks, another target attacking creature can't be blocked this turn.", 'Whenever Thieving Otter deals damage to an opponent, draw a card.', 'Whenever a creature you control deals combat damage to a player, you may draw a card.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Whenever a creature you control leaves the battlefield, if it had counters on it, put those counters on The Ozolith.\\nAt the beginning of combat on your turn, if The Ozolith has counters on it, you may move all counters from The Ozolith onto target creature.', 'Whenever a creature you control mutates, put a +1/+1 counter on that creature and you gain 2 life.', 'Whenever a non-Human creature you control attacks, look at the top six cards of your library. You may put a Human creature card from among them onto the battlefield tapped and attacking. It gains indestructible until end of turn. Put the rest of the cards on the bottom of your library in a random order.', "Whenever a nontoken creature you control dies, mill two cards. Then return a creature card with lesser mana value than the creature that died from your graveyard to your hand.\\n{1}, Sacrifice Death's Oasis: You gain life equal to the highest mana value among creatures you control.", 'Whenever this creature mutates, put a +1/+1 counter on it.', 'Whenever this creature mutates, target creature an opponent controls gets -2/-2 until end of turn.', "Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, create an X/X blue Shark creature token with flying, where X is that spell's mana value.\\nCycling {X}{1}{U} ({X}{1}{U}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)\\nWhen you cycle Shark Typhoon, create an X/X blue Shark creature token with flying.", 'Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, draw a card.', 'Whenever you cycle a card, tap target creature an opponent controls.', 'Whenever you cycle a card, you may have Reptilian Reflection become a 5/4 Dinosaur creature with trample and haste in addition to its other types until end of turn.', "Whenever you cycle a card, you may pay {1}. When you do, exile target artifact or creature you control, then return it to the battlefield under its owner's control.", 'Whenever you cycle a card, you may pay {2}. When you do, Savai Thundermane deals 2 damage to target creature and you gain 2 life.', 'Whenever you cycle another card for the first time each turn, create a 1/1 white Human Soldier creature token.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Whenever you cycle another card, Drannith Stinger deals 1 damage to each opponent.\\nCycling {1} ({1}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Whenever you cycle another card, put a +1/+1 counter on Flourishing Fox.\\nCycling {1} ({1}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Whenever you cycle another card, you gain 1 life.\\nCycling {1} ({1}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Whenever you draw a card, put a foreshadow counter on Ominous Seas.\\nRemove eight foreshadow counters from Ominous Seas: Create an 8/8 blue Kraken creature token.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Whenever you tap a nonland permanent for mana, add one mana of any type that permanent produced.\\n{5}{G}{U}: Look at the top five cards of your library. You may put a non-Human creature card from among them onto the battlefield. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order.', 'Wind-Scarred Crag enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Wind-Scarred Crag enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {W}.', "Wingfold Pteron enters the battlefield with your choice of a flying counter or a hexproof counter on it. (A creature with hexproof can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)", 'You may look at the top card of your library any time.\\nYou may cast creature spells from the top of your library.\\n[+1]: Create a 3/3 green Beast creature token. Put your choice of a vigilance counter, a reach counter, or a trample counter on it.\\n[−2]: When you next cast a creature spell this turn, search your library for a creature card with lesser mana value, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'You may play an additional land on each of your turns.\\nWhenever you cast a spell, draw two cards.\\nAt the beginning of your end step, discard your hand.', "Your opponents can't cast spells from anywhere other than their hands.", 'Zenith Flare deals X damage to any target and you gain X life, where X is the number of cards with a cycling ability in your graveyard.', '[+1]: Exile the top three cards of your library. Creature cards exiled this way gain "You may cast this card from exile as long as you control a Lukka planeswalker."\\n[−2]: Exile target creature you control, then reveal cards from the top of your library until you reveal a creature card with higher mana value. Put that card onto the battlefield and the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order.\\n[−7]: Each creature you control deals damage equal to its power to each opponent.', '[+1]: You gain 2 life. Add {U}, {R}, or {W}. Spend this mana only to cast a noncreature spell.\\n[−2]: Draw a card, then you may discard a card. When you discard a nonland card this way, Narset of the Ancient Way deals damage equal to that card\'s mana value to target creature or planeswalker.\\n[−6]: You get an emblem with "Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, this emblem deals 2 damage to any target."', "{1}, {T}, Sacrifice another creature: You gain life equal to the sacrificed creature's toughness. Draw a card.", '{1}, {T}: Blisterspit Gremlin deals 1 damage to each opponent.\\nWhenever you cast a noncreature spell, untap Blisterspit Gremlin.', '{1}, {T}: Draw a card, then discard a card.', '{1}{B}: Search your library for a card named Whisper Squad, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{1}{W}, {T}: Tap target creature.', '{2}, Sacrifice a creature: Weaponize the Monsters deals 2 damage to any target.', '{4}{B}: Return Durable Coilbug from your graveyard to your hand.', '{T}, Sacrifice Evolving Wilds: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}: Add one mana of any color. Spend this mana only to cast a creature spell.', '{T}: Add {B} or {G}.\\n{T}: Mill two cards.', '{T}: Add {B}, {G}, or {U}.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{3}, {T}: Draw a card. Activate only if you control a creature with power 4 or greater.', '{T}: Add {G}, {U}, or {R}.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', '{T}: Add {R}, {W}, or {B}.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', '{T}: Add {U}, {R}, or {W}.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', '{T}: Add {W}, {B}, or {G}.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)']
flavor: ['"A good forage if you can find it, but eat it before you get back to sanctuary. The guards won\'t let you bring it through the gates."\\n—Dennae, Savai hunter', '"Ah, we have a critic."\\n—Orthion, Lavabrink captain', '"Amazing! And I was only trying to teach her to sit!"', '"And I thought *I* had a big sweet tooth."\\n—Gannet, Skysail zoologist', '"And then the shadow took living form, and the shadow devoured the man whole—body, mind, and soul."\\n—*Tales of the Ozolith*', '"And what did we learn? Never taunt a porcuparrot!"', '"Being all-knowing is a matter of remembering which things it is crucial to forget."', '"By halves does youth depart. I remember halves of names, halves of years, halves of myself."\\n—Ogaro, wandering sage', '"Coppercoats think they understand duty and loyalty, but they can\'t begin to fathom the depths of my bond."', '"Day 1: These fox pups have really taken to me.\\n"Day 4: Big. So big. Need additional security."\\n—Jonald, mission naturalist, research notes', '"Don\'t ask me what to do if you miss. They\'re stingdrakes. Don\'t miss."\\n—Orthion, Lavabrink captain', '"Don\'t search the ruins of Orn during the day. Nethroi\'s many eyes will spot you instantly. Don\'t go at night either. You\'ll be dinner for the servals. Maybe just don\'t go."\\n—Rasai, Indatha hunter', '"Drannith gives no quarter to traitors."\\n—General Kudro', '"Every flaw in the crystal represents a moment where our strategy might go wrong."', '"Fear not the behemoth heard from miles away. Fear the stalking felidar, which reveals itself only for the kill."\\n—Rielle, the Everwise', '"Fools wear armor against it as if the worst it could take is your blood."\\n—Gavi, nest warden', '"From this day forward, we confront this world together, lifting each other up."', '"Get in there, soldier! I want a pelt on my wall before lunch!"', '"Goriaks are as stubborn and hardy as I\'d expect of a large herbivore in a wetland habitat. But I never expected them to have such beautiful voices!"\\n—Vivien Reid', '"How can you be sure you pierced its heart? Do you even know where its heart is?"\\n—Trundan, Indatha poacher', '"How did we find each other? So there I was, exploring a mound of monster corpses..."', '"How many claws does a monster have? Exactly one more than you\'ve accounted for."\\n—Alux, Skysail defender', '"I always thought wizards were supposed to have owls or one-eyed cats for familiars, but flaming dinosaurs work, too."', '"I appreciate you not letting me fall to my death in the acid bogs. Now, can you let me down?"', '"I can bring down anything in Zagoth, but for some quarry the ratio of fight to meat is too high."\\n—Master Hunter Chevill', '"I defy this world to try our defenses now. Send pterons and skycats. Send Vadrok!"\\n—Janae, Coppercoat architect', '"I have a number of hyper-specific phobias and this somehow hits all of them."\\n—Aaru, Zagoth lumberjack', '"I know the nightmares of Indatha seem scary, but when you break them down into their component parts, they\'re quite beautiful."\\n—Naireh, Ketria elementalist', '"I study bone because that\'s where truth dwells. One monster knucklebone is wiser than all that damp meat in your head."', '"I want it to look me in the eyes and know the face of the man who put it down."\\n—Kelsien, the Plague', '"I will preserve human life at all costs. I will stand alone against behemoths before I let them touch my city. I will hold the wall."\\n—Oath of the Coppercoats', '"I\'ve seen them survive lava, trampling, and a moloch\'s digestive system. They just roll out and get on with their lives!"\\n—Gannet, Skysail zoologist', '"If only they\'d all act this docile. I could do something relaxing for a living. I\'ve always wanted to bake biscuits."\\n—Ethuk, Coppercoat mage', '"If you\'ve never feasted on Zagoth terror-pig, I got the best price you\'ll find."', '"Inner peace is wonderful, and worth striving for. Outer peace is much less important."\\n—Taelya, Lavabrink pyromage', '"It\'s Snapdax. You\'d have a better chance of breaching a wall with a slice of bread."\\n—Krek, daysquad captain', '"It\'s either terrified or extremely mad at us, definitely one of the two."\\n—Jonald, mission naturalist', '"It\'s just a snake. A many-eyed snake with venom that turns your blood to smoke, but still, just a snake."\\n—Kinnan, bonder prodigy', '"It\'s not hard to grasp that this land does not belong to us."\\n—Gavi, nest warden', '"It\'s them or us."\\n—General Kudro', '"Its weak spot is easily spotted, but only if it\'s swooping down on you."\\n—Jonald, mission naturalist', '"Let the brutes fight. If they kill each other, we lose no more soldiers today."\\n—Orthion, Lavabrink captain', '"Nature is more merciless than any hunter I\'ve ever known."\\n—Zai, nightsquad captain', '"Need a medic! And some stonemasons!"\\n—Wyllon, Drannith merchant', '"No, thank you."', '"One day I woke up and knew I had nothing left to teach her. So now I ride on her shoulders and follow where she leads."\\n—Gustin, wildbonder', '"Our sanctuaries must be beacons of reason and calm or else they will fall."', '"Our volleys don\'t aim to kill. Impair them and the ground will do the rest."\\n—Alux, Skysail defender', '"Out here we\'re nothing but our training."\\n—Ethuk, Coppercoat mage', '"Sleep now, you big brute."\\n—Kelsien, the Plague', '"Stop trying to pierce the hide. Hit where it\'s softest: ankle, sole, hamstring."\\n—Master Hunter Chevill', '"Strike those abominations down. Let their names rot with their remains."\\n—General Kudro', '"Take one wrong step out here and you\'re dead. I take only right steps."', '"Take us home," she whispered, and the fox\'s eyes began to glow.', '"Talk later. Row now!"', '"The *eludha* is total communication, total understanding. It makes regular human speech feel like garbled grunting."\\n—Winota, heartbonder', '"The big fella sounds hungry. Let\'s send him to bed without his supper."', '"The bonders work with creatures that fly, slink, and burrow. Assume they know everything."\\n—Jirina Kudro', '"The cruelest monsters inspire the greatest tales. The greatest tales inspire the cruelest hunters."\\n—Rielle, the Everwise', '"The endurance of the ancient turtles in a land so harsh makes a strong case for patience, tranquility, and composure."\\n—Gavi, nest warden', '"The glowstones shine and dinosaurs roar to the south. Business will be brisk tonight."', '"The ground under our feet is a record of every slight against the world, to be avenged at a time of its choosing."\\n—Gavi, nest warden', '"The key to bonding with monsters, no matter their size, is knowing where they like to be scratched."', '"The monster that scares me the most isn\'t the biggest."\\n—Taelya, Lavabrink pyromage', '"The most unexpected weapon that a monster can wield is kindness."\\n—*Tales of the Ozolith*', '"The night emboldens many monsters, but the mightiest will attack in broad daylight."', '"The poacher\'s trade isn\'t monster parts. It\'s myth. People pay to be part of the fantasy."\\n—Kelsien, the Plague', '"Their paths aren\'t random, but they don\'t float with the wind. Could they be following surges in crystalline energy?"\\n—Naireh, Ketria elementalist', '"There is no law of nature that I have not seen Illuna break. Makes you wonder what is truly possible, does it not?"\\n—Rielle, the Everwise', '"There\'s no roar so mighty that it can\'t be silenced."', '"These lowlands were formed thousands of years ago by the behemoth Indath—its final footsteps before vanishing into the sea."\\n—*Tales of the Ozolith*', '"They cast wards, thinking it will protect them, but the biggest monsters find a way through."\\n—Kinnan, bonder prodigy', '"They say it survives on a purely bioluminescent diet. It\'s only active during the darkest of Indatha nights, making verification highly challenging."\\n—Gannet, Skysail zoologist', '"Though the road through Raugrin is lined with alarm crystals, some monsters seem to be adapting. We\'ve had raptors feigning attacks on provision caravans, while others try to sneak through the lava curtain."\\n—Dol, Lavabrink quartermaster', '"Turns out the case of the flattened outpost and the case of the missing kitten *were* related."\\n—Endris, Drannith magistrate', '"Water and bone tell many tales, but fire is fickle. It would rather consume than reveal."\\n—Rielle, the Everwise', '"We are each other\'s shadow, fleeting yet always present."', '"We share the same nuanced opinion of hunters and military goons: smash them."', '"What she sees, I see. What she tastes, I taste."', '"What\'s natural on Ikoria continues to delight me."\\n—Vivien Reid', '"When monsters walk, the earth knows its place and yields."\\n—Rielle, the Everwise', '"With the frequent mutations, predator-prey relationships seem to change every moment. I already like it here."\\n—Vivien Reid', '"World\'s better with one fewer poacher in it."\\n—Winota, heartbonder', '"Yesterday it was flying tigers and crumbling bridges. Who knows what today will bring?"\\n—Dol, Lavabrink quartermaster', '"You sure you want to see what emerges? You might not like it. It definitely won\'t like you."\\n—Kinnan, bonder prodigy', '"You\'re little now, yes, but one day your footsteps will make mountains tremble."\\n—Gustin, wildbonder', '"You\'re not my quarry, little one. I\'m after whatever comes to investigate your cries."\\n—Kelsien, the Plague', '"You\'re telling me we spent a year securing the sanctuary against pterosaurs, rambeasts, and nightfangs . . . and we were robbed by what?"\\n—Endris, Drannith magistrate', '"You\'ve never had to trust your breath to an inhuman creature who could crush you at its whim, and I truly feel sorry for you."\\n—Eagan, seabonder', '"Your prey is in my custody now. Withdraw."\\n—Vivien Reid', 'A crackling roar is the last sound many hunters hear.', "After a disastrous day of battle, Lavabrink's lightning mages were recalled.", 'After much arguing, the soldiers decided to keep it, on the grounds that it killed enough mice to count as an honorary monster slayer.', "After what he viewed as Lukka's shocking betrayal, General Kudro enacted stringent security measures at every entry point into Drannith.", "All they found in the hunter's camp were tiny paw prints and a lot of blood.", 'An adventure without a companion is hardly an adventure at all.', 'As Narset struggled to meditate, tiny dragonlings spiraled around her, conjuring thoughts of ancient clans.', 'As it twists, so does all life around it.', "Bonder and bonded move in unison, intuiting each other's next move.", 'Broad prairies feed the human sanctuary of Drannith and conceal a network of caverns where giant cats make their dens.', "Considering the zealous armies, vile poachers, and titanic monsters, it's always wise to keep one eye on the horizon.", "Crystals nestle in the roots of Indatha's helica trees as if being nurtured by their embrace.", 'Danger often lurks in the allure of crystal shards.', "Each scorpion's venom is unique, thwarting sanctuary healers' attempts to develop an antidote.", "Ears can't hear them. Eyes see too many of them.", 'Fear is its habitat, sanity its prey.', 'Fear pierces the strongest armor.', 'Few monsters challenged Narset after they sensed her power.', "For safety reasons, the keeping of houseplants within Ikoria's sanctuaries is heavily discouraged.", 'Fortune favors the ferocious.', 'Fragile, floating Skysail suddenly seemed like an appealingly safe place to live.', "From a certain perspective, it's an inspiring story of overcoming obstacles.", 'From now until the crystals stop glowing\\n—Ketria oath meaning "forever"', 'From the fertile muck of Zagoth, everything—animal, botanical, and crystalline—grows with rugged beauty.', 'Hunter and hunted both died thinking they had outwitted the other.', 'Hunters in the primeval wetlands become fluent in reading the ripples to tell when to pursue and when to flee.', "Hunters' methods vary from simple and brutal to elaborate and brutal.", 'If you feel a strange chill within the temperate Quartzwood, look up.', 'It always knew it was destined to be more than a frog.', 'It could subsist on seeds but its preferred fare is your face.', 'It loves blending into its environment, ambushing prey, and long scuttles on the beach.', 'It makes molehills out of mountains.', 'It soars through currents of moonbeams to give hope to the forsaken.', 'Laughed at the brushwagg\\n—Hunters\' expression meaning "died unexpectedly"', "Lavabrink's boiling moat is a deterrent for most, and a relaxing bath for one.", 'Life is best taken one step at a time.', 'Lives taken are lives not easily forgotten.', 'Lukka looked out from the parapet and saw not a monster to be put down, but a fierce kind of beauty.', 'Lukka was ordered to kill a threat. He chose to make a friend.', "Lukka's bond provided not only friendship, but also the most powerful weapon in his arsenal.", "More stubborn than Drannith's walls.", 'Most monsters are more frightening when they skitter unseen in the dark. Most.', 'No human eyes have ever witnessed the birth of an apex monster.', 'Nothing returns from the nightmare nests of Indatha unscathed.', 'Nowhere on Ikoria are monsters more integral to the landscape than Ketria, where the river itself will stand up and roar.', 'On Ikoria, reactive magic can make the difference between barely grazed and really dead.', 'On Ikoria, sandwurms never lie dormant for too long. In some regions, "no activity" is the greatest sign of danger.', "Outside Drannith's walls, where collateral damage is of no concern, the Coppercoats are free to use more potent methods.", 'Poachers use the harvested tongues to snare pests, plumb caves, and scale tall buildings.', 'Raugrin meets the sea with jaws wide, its coast spiked with teeth of crystal and granite.', "Raugrin's coastline can be quite beautiful, as long as you avoid the volcanic dinosaurs, the sea dinosaurs, and the roaming beach dinosaurs.", 'Remarkably, dinner continued with no further interruptions.', 'Revenge is a path inevitably walked alone.', "Sanctuaries harnessed the glowstones' natural reaction to monsters to create a warning system.", "Scavengers follow in Skysail's shadow, feasting on the carcasses of monsters that attacked the floating city.", 'She was born unable to walk. Through the *eludha*, she was able to fly.', 'She wept, not from perfect understanding, but from serene gratitude.', 'Size of a pixie, rage of a hellkite.', "Skysail's strength was also its vulnerability.", 'Some crystals glow in the presence of monsters, forming a convenient warning system. Some monsters have learned to outrun the light.', 'Sometimes the *eludha* is a sacred harmony of souls. Sometimes the bonder grabs some fur and holds on tight.', "The Ozolith's appearance spawned a new era of wild mutation on Ikoria. Some creatures hunted different prey, lived in new habitats, and thrived on mutation itself.", 'The Wanderer walks many paths. Her blade travels only one.', "The Zagoth wetlands are fertilized by centuries of Brokkos's former challengers.", 'The bounty on its head is as old as Skysail, but no one has ever tried to collect.', 'The call of the wild is rarely a solo.', 'The dark of night never truly falls on Ketria, where abundant crystals bathe the land in their glow.', 'The definition of "bite-sized treat" depends on who you ask.', 'The first line of defense, and the last person you want to anger.', "The floating city of Skysail has two rules: don't leave your crewmates behind, and don't mess with the guardrails.", "The giant tigers of Savai prefer to hunt at daybreak, when the crystals' warning glow is masked by the light of dawn.", "The living fear Nethroi's whispers. The dead heed them.", "The same crystals that root deep enough to pierce Savai's catacombs also soar high enough to change its weather.", 'The soldier had given up his wealth, his title, even his home, but he had no room for regret. At last, he had saved his friend.', "The sound of Vadrok's gigantic wings is ominous. But the true terror is when they fall silent.", 'The two looked at each other, and neither fled. "I see," the soldier murmured. "We\'re both just fighting for survival out here, aren\'t we?"', 'The vegetation in Raugrin is dull, but that only makes the towering crystal structures gleam brighter.', 'Their bond grew over time, as did the height of their jumps.', 'Their feeding habits leave them with gizzards full of tumbled gems.', 'There is a sanctuary that reveals itself only to those graced by the *eludha*—the mystical connection between bonder and monster.', 'There is no boat big enough.', 'Through the *eludha*, bonders share the powerful abilities of their chosen companions.']
